CONDITIONAL ROUTES (CDR)
CDRs are ATS routes which are usable only under
specified conditions. Three types of Conditional
Routes are used as described below:
a. CDR1 - an ATS route (or part of ATS route)
available for flight planning as published in
Jeppesen Enroute “Airway Restrictions - East-
ern Europe Lower and Upper Airspace”;
b. CDR2 - an ATS route (or part of ATS route)
available for flight planning as published in the
Airspace Availability Bulletin (AAB);
c. CDR3 - an ATS route (or part of ATS route)
only available with ATC unit clearance.
CDR1 and CDR2 shall be indicated in the flight plan,
if the time when its planned to use the specified con-
ditional route is consistent with the time published in
the aeronautical information documents. CDR3 are
not plannable.
If CDR1 and CDR2 are established on one segment
of the ATS route within the same vertical limits, the
time periods, when CDR2 can be available for flight
planning according to the AAB, shall be indicated in
the Restrictions column of Jeppesen Enroute “Air-
way Restrictions - Eastern Europe Lower and Upper
Airspace”. For example:
–
CDR1: FL450-FL530 SUN and HOL (CDR1 is
available for flight planning on the specified days);
–
CDR2: FL450-FL530 other days (CDR2 is avail-
able for flight planning on any day, except SUN
and HOL, according to the AAB).
